cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Composite Indices Are Policies, Not Measures"
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Lam"
    given-names: "Brendan"
    email: "brendannathanlam@hotmail.com"
    affiliation: "Yale University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/blam3/composite-indices-as-policies"
abstract: >-
  Tools and analyses treating area-level allocation composites such as the
  CDC/ATSDR Social Vulnerability Index as policies rather than measures.
  Includes an exact reproduction of the SVI 2022 pipeline and a
  decision-reliability analysis based on ACS variance replicate estimates.
keywords:
  - composite indicators
  - social vulnerability index
  - measurement error
  - policy learning
  - American Community Survey
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-08-22"
